## 👥 3. The Staff Identity Flow (SSO Sync)

Staff identity is split between two systems: **Authentik** (the Identity Provider handling passwords/MFA) and **Supabase** (the database holding roles and permissions).

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Authentik IdP] -->|SAML/OIDC Login| B[Supabase `auth.users`]
    B -->|Manual Profile Creation| C[Supabase `public.users`]
```

1. **Provision in Authentik:** Create the staff member (e.g., `dr.sharma@cityhospital.local`) in the Authentik Admin UI.
2. **First Login:** The staff member logs into StayAssist via SSO. This automatically generates a row in Supabase's secure `auth.users` table.
3. **Get Auth UUID:** Query Supabase to find their auto-generated auth UUID.
   ```sql
   SELECT id FROM auth.users WHERE email = 'dr.sharma@cityhospital.local';
   -- 📌 COPY THIS UUID (We will call it <AUTH_ID>)
   ```
4. **Create App Profile & Role:** Link the auth identity to the hospital and department.
   ```sql
   INSERT INTO public.users (id, email, first_name, last_name, role, department_id, hospital_id, mfa_enabled, is_active)
   VALUES (
     '<AUTH_ID>', -- MUST MATCH EXACTLY
     'dr.sharma@cityhospital.local',
     'Priya', 'Sharma',
     'quality_coordinator',
     '<DEPT_ID>',
     '<HOSPITAL_ID>',
     TRUE, TRUE
   );
   ```

*(Once the staff member has a profile in `public.users`, Row-Level Security (RLS) policies will allow them to see the dashboard).*

